    [Doc][Misc] Standardize memory units and clean up model deployment tutorials (#19609)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    This PR updates and cleans up several model deployment tutorials for
    Ascend hardware (including DeepSeek-V4-Pro, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash,
    Qwen3.5-397B-A17B, Qwen3.5-Dense, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, and
    Qwen3.8-Flash-Next).
    
    - Standardizes memory unit representations from \"G\" to \"GB\" (e.g.,
    \"64G\" to \"64GB\", \"96G\" to \"96GB\") to ensure professional and
    consistent terminology.
    - Removes trailing whitespaces across multiple markdown files.
    - Updates the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next tutorial to reflect the correct
    validation baseline (`vllm-ascend:v0.26.0rc`) and removes outdated
    hardware support notes.
    - Corrects port configurations in the DeepSeek-V4-Pro disaggregated
    deployment example.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No. This is a documentation-only update.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    No functional code changes; verified markdown rendering.
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [ ] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: I reviewed whether this change
    involves
    boundary conditions (e.g. empty input, single/zero element, min/max
    values,
    off-by-one, sequence-length limits, integer overflow). Where applicable,
    I
    added unit tests covering these edge cases in `tests/ut/` or
    `tests/e2e/`.
    - [ ] **Regression test**: If this PR fixes a bug, I added a regression
    test
      that would fail without the fix.
    - [ ] **Error / failure path coverage**: I covered abnormal paths
    (exceptions,
    timeouts, out-of-range, division by zero) in addition to the happy path.
    - [ ] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: New tests assert real behavior
    and are
      not written merely to satisfy CI.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: If this PR touches a performance-sensitive
    path,
      I attached benchmark results and added performance regression tests.
    
    
